@startuml AIVAS System Architecture
title AIVAS - Deployment Architecture (Vercel + Supabase + GitHub)
left to right direction

package "Clients" {
  [PPIC Portal (Web)] as ppic
  [Vendor Portal (Web)] as vendor
  [Inbound Scanner App (Mobile/Browser)] as scanner
  [Supervisor Dashboard (Web)] as supervisor
}

node "Vercel" as vercel {
  component "Frontend (Next.js on Vercel)" as frontend
  component "Serverless API (Next.js API Routes / Edge Functions)" as api
  ' component "Background Jobs / Scheduled Functions" as jobs
}

database "Supabase (Postgres)" as db
cloud "Supabase Storage (Object Storage)" as storage


node "GitHub (Repo)" as github

vendor --> frontend : Uses
scanner --> frontend : Uses (offline queue + sync)
supervisor --> frontend : Uses

ppic --> frontend : Uses

frontend --> api : API calls (HTTPS)
api --> db : Read / Write
api --> storage : Upload / Download photos
' jobs --> db : background writes (tickets, audit)
' jobs --> storage : image processing / thumbnails

github --> vercel : Push to main triggers Vercel build & deploy

' note bottom of storage
'   Photo/attachment storage: Supabase Storage (S3 compatible). DB stores URLs and metadata only.
' end note

' note right of api
'   - Verify QR signature (HMAC)
'   - Idempotency for scan receipts
'   - Rate-limit and RBAC checks
' end note

' note top of github
'   - GitHub holds source; Vercel automatically builds & deploys on push to configured branches.
'   - Use GitHub Actions only for CI, pre-merge checks, or migration jobs (optional).
' end note

' note left of db
'   - Supabase used only for Postgres and Object Storage in this deployment.
'   - Authentication is handled separately (not Supabase Auth).
' end note

@enduml
